+  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 3 introduces several mechanics not present in L1/L2 banked knowledge: (1) a per-level ACTION TIMER rendered as the bottom status row depleting 1 cell per 2 actions (64 cells = ~128 action budget); (2) a mobile x-colored BLOCKER (5x5 head + 3-wide tongue on a horizontal track spanning the corridor rows 20-24) that docks in the right shaft blocking descent, and slides one dock left toward the player when the player enters its track band - clearing the right shaft; (3) two-position ELEVATOR CARS ('+' colored 5x5 blocks on vertical wires) that block passages at their default dock and slide one quantum away while a body stands on their call plate, snapping back the moment the plate is released; (4) full CLONE COMMIT/REWIND semantics for ACTION5: pressing 5 commits the current trajectory, rewinds the active player to level spawn, and the committed ghost (rendered in color 2) REPLAYS its trajectory one action per subsequent player action, then parks at its endpoint FOREVER - parked ghosts hold plates (this is what 'clone holds the plate' meant in the L2 registry notes); 3 run slots total (2 commits + final run), shown top-left; committing an EMPTY trajectory (5 at spawn with no moves) does NOT consume a slot; (5) the goal is the 7x7 ring with a center dot at (19,19)-(25,25): the win fired exactly when the active player filled its 5x5 interior (top-left (20,20)), consistent with the registry's player==target+offset predicate.",
